A||N||4||Haze_Performance||Will they fit?||||5||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||03-21-2000||11:25 PM||||Anyone know if the 2000 Grand Am wheels will fit my 1985 2M4? I know that the 1995 Grand Am wheels should fit but how about the 2000's. Did pontiac change the lug pattern? I would like to bolt on a set of the 2000 16" Chrome 5 stars with the factory pontiac emblem.||||reg||5
Z||000001||ChadMan||03-22-2000||09:39 AM||||I'm 99% sure the bolt pattern is the same, but the offset is a little different since the wheels were designed for an FWD car.  If they're 16x6 wheels, you should have no problem, but if they're 16x7, you may have clearance problems with suspension components.<P>If you're buying them from a local boneyard, they'd probably let you bring them back if they didn't fit - or let you test-fit one in their parking lot!||||reg||1
Z||000002||TalShino||03-22-2000||09:55 AM||||isn't the Fiero a FWD car?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> atleast it has a FWD offset or whatnot dont it?<P>Tal Shino||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChadMan||03-22-2000||10:08 AM||||While the Fiero uses GM FWD drivetrains, it's not a FWD car, and the wheel offsets really were different on Fieros than on GM FWD cars.  If you look closely at a set of 14" alloys for a mid-80's Sunbird/Grand Am, you'll note that the face of the wheel is flush with the rim...similar wheels on the Fiero have a 1/2" lip so the face of the wheel is slightly recessed.  A set of Fiero wheels would stick out slightly past the fender on a Sunbird.<P>It's my understanding that using wheels with the wrong offset can cause handling problems with FWD cars, but the effects aren't as serious with RWD cars like the Fiero (c'mon, tech guys, help me out here).||||reg||1
Z||000004||ChadMan||03-22-2000||10:23 AM||||This car belongs to a guy from Central Ohio Fiero Enthusiasts - a true Fieroholic.<P>Here it is with 15" Fiero wheels:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/86sefrontleft.jpg"> <P>Here it is with 16" Z24 wheels:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/86se99c.jpg"> <P>The Cavvy wheels look cool, but see how they look more "tucked into" the bodywork than the Fiero wheels?||||reg||1
